    "case_id": "310",
    "case_summary": "An elderly man presented to the emergency department after falling out of bed with quadriplegia, urinary and stool incontinence, and hypothermia (temperature, 33.1°C).\n\nPhysical examination revealed:- Absent rectal tone- Complete sensory loss- Quadriplegia- Temperature: 33.1°C- Urinary and stool incontinence\n\n- MRI of cervical spine:  Image Title: Magnetic Resonance Imaging of the Cervical Spine  Image Description: Showed anterior and posterior longitudinal ligament, ligamentum flavum, and interspinous disruptions at C4 and C5 with spinal cord compression with anterolisthesis.- Diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI):  Image Title: Axial Diffusion-Weighted Imaging  Image Description: Revealed abnormally hyperintense spinal cord white matter, reflecting reduced diffusion, which outlines the hypointense signal of central gray matter. At the level of C5 and C6, reduced diffusion in the spinal cord white matter, outlining a hypointense signal of the central gray matter.",
